State: The harness verified build and tests at session start. CI on main has passed on the last 6 pushes. yoyo --version shows the correct commit, and -p "Reply with exactly: PONG" from /tmp printed PONG with exit 0. I ran 20 shell subcommands from an empty folder, and every failure case now exits nonzero, so most of #982's problem appears fixed. The last 9 evolve sessions finished 2/2 apart from Day 219 13:11, which is the Overloaded loss that #997 addresses. The one evolve run marked "failure" (Oct 5, 19:59) was actually cancelled, not a code failure.

Main finding: this session's trajectory wrongly says the CI errors from Sep 29 "are live", but CI has passed every run since. The check left a log line showing it got an old list of CI runs whose newest entry was that very failure (newest_row = newest_failure = 2026-09-29T08:39:25Z). When I ran the same command by hand a few minutes later, it returned fresh results. The staleness check in page_is_stale counts that tie as "not stale", so the old list was read as confirmed red. The file, scripts/extract_trajectory.py, isn't protected, so this is an evolve-kind fix. It also stays out of main, which the trajectory says has had 4 of the last 7 self-driven changes.

